@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `il-interpretation-time`
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g7-fourth-schedule`
IMPORT `g7-commencement`

-- g7-tests-commencement.l4: tests of section 63 (commencement and application).
--
-- Written by ENCODER G7.  Every expected date below was decided from the SOURCE before any run, by counting with the
-- Interpretation Law s.10 as the vendored module states it, and then compared with the survey's own pre-computed
-- chain (which was made with a Python calendar and not with the module):
--   * the Law was published in Reshumot on 14.1.2025 (the gazette's date line); the Knesset passed it on 8.1.2025;
--   * three months after 14.1.2025 end on 14.4.2025 (IL s.10(b): the same-numbered day), a Monday;
--   * the regulations under section 59 came into force on 16.7.2025 (regulation 5 of the Fees Regulations: 7 days
--     from the publication of 9.7.2025, IL s.10(a); and the wiki's own note on section 63(a)(1)), a Wednesday;
--   * the commencement day is the later of the two: 16.7.2025;
--   * 18 months after 16.7.2025 end on 16.1.2027 (same-numbered day), a Saturday; its day after is 17.1.2027;
--   * three years after 16.7.2025 end on 16.7.2028, a Sunday (pinned in the Interpretation NOTES answer table).
-- Dates that are not the sources' own are hypothetical and say so; they exist to put one date on each side of an edge.
--
-- Weekdays used below, from the calendar: 14.1.2025 Tuesday, 14.4.2025 Monday, 16.7.2025 Wednesday, 16.1.2027 Saturday,
-- 17.1.2027 Sunday.  The calendars of rest days in these tests are ILLUSTRATIONS and not a statement of any calendar.

§ `Tests of section 63`

§§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN pub IS A DATE
      regs59 IS A DATE
      regs46 IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts: published on` pub `, section 59 regulations in force on` regs59 `, section 46 regulations in force on` regs46 MEANS
    `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63` WITH
        `the day the Law was published in Reshumot` IS pub
        `the s.59 regulations came into force on` IS regs59
        `the day regulations under section 46 came into force, if any` IS regs46

-- The facts as the sources give them: published 14.1.2025, section 59 regulations in force 16.7.2025, no section 46 regulation.
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts as the sources give them` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING

-- Hypothetical: the section 59 regulations in force EARLY, on 1.3.2025, before three months from publication are up.
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING

-- Hypothetical: published 31.1.2025 (so three months end on the month's last day), regulations in force early.
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts published on the last day of January` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 31) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING

-- Hypothetical: the section 59 regulations in force on 31.8.2025, so 18 months later is a month with no 31st.
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts with the regulations in force on the last day of August` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 8 31) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING

-- The Knesset passed the Law on 8.1.2025: the other candidate for "its publication" (fork F-C-2), with the early regulations.
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts counted from the day the Knesset passed the Law` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 8) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 3 1) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING

-- Hypothetical section 46 regulations: in force on 1.6.2026 (before the first limb of 63(b) ends) and on 1.3.2027 (after).
GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts with section 46 regulations in force before the first limb ends` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, section 46 regulations in force on` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1))

GIVETH A `Facts that fix the commencement of the Law under section 63`
`the facts with section 46 regulations in force after the first limb ends` MEANS
    `the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, section 46 regulations in force on` (JUST (YMD 2027 3 1))

-- A calendar of rest days that holds only Saturday 16.1.2027 (illustrative).
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`the calendar with Saturday 16 January 2027 as a day of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2027 1 16

-- A calendar of rest days that holds Monday 14.4.2025 and Tuesday 15.4.2025 (illustrative, hypothetical).
GIVETH A `Calendar of rest days`
`the calendar with 14 and 15 April 2025 as days of rest` MEANS
    `Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS LIST YMD 2025 4 14, YMD 2025 4 15

-- The refrigerants.
GIVETH A Refrigerant
`lawful propane` MEANS Refrigerant OF "290", TRUE
GIVETH A Refrigerant
`unlawful propane` MEANS Refrigerant OF "290", FALSE
GIVETH A Refrigerant
`lawful isobutane` MEANS Refrigerant OF "600a", TRUE
GIVETH A Refrigerant
`unlawful isobutane` MEANS Refrigerant OF "600a", FALSE
GIVETH A Refrigerant
`lawful R134a` MEANS Refrigerant OF "134a", TRUE
GIVETH A Refrigerant
`a lawful gas the Schedule does not list` MEANS Refrigerant OF "9999", TRUE

-- The systems (the capacity is not a question of section 63 and is the same throughout).
GIVEN refrigerants IS A LIST OF Refrigerant
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system operating by` refrigerants MEANS
    `Cooling system` WITH
        `cooling capacity in kilowatts` IS 12
        `refrigerants` IS refrigerants

GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with propane only` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `lawful propane`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with R134a only` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `lawful R134a`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with an unlisted gas only` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `a lawful gas the Schedule does not list`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with unlawful propane only` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `unlawful propane`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with propane and isobutane` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `lawful propane`, `lawful isobutane`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with propane and R134a` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `lawful propane`, `lawful R134a`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with R134a and an unlisted gas` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `lawful R134a`, `a lawful gas the Schedule does not list`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with unlawful propane and R134a` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `unlawful propane`, `lawful R134a`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with lawful propane and unlawful isobutane` MEANS `a system operating by` (LIST `lawful propane`, `unlawful isobutane`)
GIVETH A `Cooling system`
`a system with no refrigerant recorded` MEANS `a system operating by` EMPTY

-- Whether the Law has commenced for work on a system on a day, on the facts as the sources give them.
GIVEN system IS A `Cooling system`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`work on` system `on` day MEANS
    `the Law has commenced for work on the system` system `on the day` day `given the facts` `the facts as the sources give them`

§§ `63(a)(1). The commencement day: the later of three months from publication and the regulations`

-- The chain from the sources: 14.4.2025 against 16.7.2025, the later being 16.7.2025.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts as the sources give them` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16

-- The first limb alone: three months after the publication day, IL s.10(b), the same-numbered day.
-- (With the regulations in force on 1.3.2025 the first limb is the later: 14.4.2025.)
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14
-- Month-end: three months after 31.1.2025 end on 30.4.2025, the month's last day (IL s.10(b)).
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts published on the last day of January` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 30

-- The edge: the regulations in force on the very day the three months end, and one day later.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 4 14) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 4 15) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 15
-- And one day before: the three months are the later.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 4 13) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 14

-- The three years of the Second Schedule's notes run from the commencement day of paragraph (1), not from paragraph (2)'s
-- date (trap T7): 16.7.2025 plus three years is 16.7.2028, a Sunday; counted from paragraph (2)'s date it would be 16.1.2030.
#ASSERT `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (`the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts as the sources give them`) EQUALS YMD 2028 7 16
#ASSERT `s 10(b) — the last day of a period of` 3 `years after an event on` (`the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant under section 63(a)(2)` `the facts as the sources give them`) EQUALS YMD 2030 1 16

§§ `63(a)(2). Eighteen months from the commencement day`

#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant under section 63(a)(2)` `the facts as the sources give them` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
-- Month-end: 18 months after 31.8.2025 end on 28.2.2027 (February 2027 has 28 days).
#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant under section 63(a)(2)` `the facts with the regulations in force on the last day of August` EQUALS YMD 2027 2 28
-- 18 months after the early commencement day 14.4.2025 end on 14.10.2026.
#ASSERT `the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant under section 63(a)(2)` `the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` EQUALS YMD 2026 10 14

§§ `63(a). Whether the Law has commenced for work on a system on a day`

-- A system with a lawful propane (paragraph (1)): from the commencement day, 16.7.2025, on.
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with propane only` `on` (YMD 2025 1 14) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with propane only` `on` (YMD 2025 7 15) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with propane only` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with propane only` `on` (YMD 2025 7 17) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with propane only` `on` (YMD 2027 1 16) EQUALS TRUE

-- Isobutane 600a and the other numeric and lower-case designations are listed too.
#ASSERT `work on` (`a system operating by` (LIST `lawful isobutane`)) `on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `work on` (`a system operating by` (LIST `lawful isobutane`)) `on` (YMD 2025 7 15) EQUALS FALSE

-- A system with a refrigerant the Schedule does not list (paragraph (2)): 18 months later, 16.1.2027.
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with R134a only` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with R134a only` `on` (YMD 2026 12 31) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with R134a only` `on` (YMD 2027 1 15) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with R134a only` `on` (YMD 2027 1 16) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with R134a only` `on` (YMD 2027 1 17) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with an unlisted gas only` `on` (YMD 2027 1 15) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with an unlisted gas only` `on` (YMD 2027 1 16) EQUALS TRUE

-- Before the commencement day nothing has commenced, whatever the refrigerant: the publication day itself, too.
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with R134a only` `on` (YMD 2025 1 14) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with R134a only` `on` (YMD 2025 4 14) EQUALS FALSE

-- Paragraph (1) takes a lawful use: a listed propane whose use is not permitted is "not as stated in paragraph (1)", so
-- on the words of paragraph (2) it falls to the later date (fork F-C-6b, reading taken).
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with unlawful propane only` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with unlawful propane only` `on` (YMD 2027 1 15) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with unlawful propane only` `on` (YMD 2027 1 16) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `The regime of a system`

#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with propane only` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (1)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with propane and isobutane` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (1)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with R134a only` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with an unlisted gas only` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with R134a and an unlisted gas` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with unlawful propane only` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with unlawful propane and R134a` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (2)`
-- A system with a lawful and a listed-but-unlawful refrigerant has one refrigerant of paragraph (1): paragraph (1) governs it
-- on the reading taken (any refrigerant as stated in it).
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with lawful propane and unlawful isobutane` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (1)`
#ASSERT `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with propane and R134a` EQUALS `the regime of paragraph (1)`

-- No refrigerant recorded: the text classifies a system by its refrigerant, so there is no classification.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the regime of a system under section 63(a)` `a system with no refrigerant recorded` BECAUSE "no refrigerant is recorded for the system, and section 63(a) classifies a system by its refrigerant"

§§ `A system with no refrigerant recorded: refused only where the answer depends on the regime`

-- Before the commencement day nothing has commenced, and from the day paragraph (2) takes effect both have: no need to classify.
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with no refrigerant recorded` `on` (YMD 2025 7 15) EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with no refrigerant recorded` `on` (YMD 2027 1 16) EQUALS TRUE
-- Between the two, the regime decides and the text does not give it.
#ASSERT REFUSED `work on` `a system with no refrigerant recorded` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16) BECAUSE "no refrigerant is recorded for the system, and section 63(a) classifies a system by its refrigerant"
#ASSERT REFUSED `work on` `a system with no refrigerant recorded` `on` (YMD 2027 1 15) BECAUSE "no refrigerant is recorded for the system, and section 63(a) classifies a system by its refrigerant"

§§ `The work item wrapper (IP2)`

`a propane work item` MEANS `Work item` WITH
    `performed by` IS `Person` WITH `reference for the person` IS "p-1", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
    `the kind of job` IS `an installation job`
    `the system` IS `a system with propane only`
    `date performed` IS YMD 2025 7 16

#ASSERT `the Law has commenced for the work item` `a propane work item` `given the facts` `the facts as the sources give them`

§§ `63(a)(1), last clause: the Minister's power to amend the Fourth Schedule`

#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the consultation needed for an order amending the Fourth Schedule has taken place` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 63(a)(1) — the consultation needed for an order amending the Fourth Schedule has taken place` FALSE
#TRACE `s 63(a)(1) — the Minister's power to amend the Fourth Schedule by order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `amend the Fourth Schedule by order` AT 9
#TRACE `s 63(a)(1) — the Minister's power to amend the Fourth Schedule by order` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    -- not consulted: no permission

§§ `63(a). The provisions that are not about work on a system (trap T20): no day is given`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the Law has commenced, for a provision that is not about work on a system, on the day` (YMD 2025 7 16) BECAUSE "section 63(a) fixes a commencement only for the performance of work on a system, and gives no day for the other provisions of the Law"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Law has commenced, for a provision that is not about work on a system, on the day` (YMD 2030 1 1) BECAUSE "section 63(a) fixes a commencement only for the performance of work on a system, and gives no day for the other provisions of the Law"

§§ `63(b). Chapter 6`

-- The first limb: 18 months from the commencement day, 16.1.2027.
-- With no section 46 regulation known, the later date does not exist: the day Chapter 6 commences is a named refusal.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` `the facts as the sources give them` BECAUSE "section 63(b) starts Chapter 6 at the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46, and none are in the sources"
-- Section 46 regulations in force BEFORE the first limb ends: the first limb is the later, 16.1.2027.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force before the first limb ends` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
-- Section 46 regulations in force AFTER the first limb ends: their day is the later, 1.3.2027.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force after the first limb ends` EQUALS YMD 2027 3 1
-- On the very day: the two limbs coincide.
#ASSERT `the day Chapter 6 commences under section 63(b)` (`the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 14) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, section 46 regulations in force on` (JUST (YMD 2027 1 16))) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16

-- Whether Chapter 6 was in force on a day (PLAN IP16).  Before the first limb ends it was not, whatever section 46 says.
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 15) `given the facts` `the facts as the sources give them` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2025 7 16) `given the facts` `the facts as the sources give them` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 15) `given the facts` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force before the first limb ends` EQUALS FALSE
-- From the first limb on, with no section 46 regulation known, whether Chapter 6 was in force is not answered by the sources.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 16) `given the facts` `the facts as the sources give them` BECAUSE "section 63(b) starts Chapter 6 at the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46, and none are in the sources"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2030 1 1) `given the facts` `the facts as the sources give them` BECAUSE "section 63(b) starts Chapter 6 at the later of 18 months from the commencement day and the entry into force of regulations under section 46, and none are in the sources"
-- With section 46 regulations known: later of the two.
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 1 16) `given the facts` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force before the first limb ends` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 2 28) `given the facts` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force after the first limb ends` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 3 1) `given the facts` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force after the first limb ends` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `Chapter 6 was in force on the day of the act` (YMD 2027 3 2) `given the facts` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force after the first limb ends` EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Fork F-C-1: IL s.10(c) applied to a period counted from another date (alternative, not taken)`

-- Paragraph (2)'s day, 16.1.2027, is a Saturday.  With the Saturday as a day of rest, IL s.10(c) moves the end to Sunday 17.1.2027.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` `the facts as the sources give them` (`the readings of the dates with IL s.10(c) applied, for the calendar` `the calendar with Saturday 16 January 2027 as a day of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 17
-- With no rest day on it, IL s.10(c) changes nothing: the same 16.1.2027.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` `the facts as the sources give them` (`the readings of the dates with IL s.10(c) applied, for the calendar` (`Calendar of rest days` WITH `days of rest, recess or holiday` IS EMPTY)) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 16
-- The first limb too: three months after 14.1.2025 end on Monday 14.4.2025; with that and the next day as rest days, the end is 16.4.2025.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` `the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` (`the readings of the dates with IL s.10(c) applied, for the calendar` `the calendar with 14 and 15 April 2025 as days of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2025 4 16
-- Applied to Chapter 6's first limb as well.
#ASSERT `s 63(b) — the day Chapter 6 commences, under the readings` `the facts with section 46 regulations in force before the first limb ends` (`the readings of the dates with IL s.10(c) applied, for the calendar` `the calendar with Saturday 16 January 2027 as a day of rest`) EQUALS YMD 2027 1 17
-- Work on a system of paragraph (2): on the reading with IL s.10(c) applied the Law has NOT commenced on Saturday 16.1.2027 but has on 17.1.2027.
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with R134a only` (YMD 2027 1 16) `the facts as the sources give them` (`the readings of the dates with IL s.10(c) applied, for the calendar` `the calendar with Saturday 16 January 2027 as a day of rest`) `the readings of the regime taken` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with R134a only` (YMD 2027 1 17) `the facts as the sources give them` (`the readings of the dates with IL s.10(c) applied, for the calendar` `the calendar with Saturday 16 January 2027 as a day of rest`) `the readings of the regime taken` EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Fork F-C-2: its publication, or the day the Knesset passed it (alternative, not taken)`

-- Counted from 8.1.2025 the three months end on 8.4.2025 (Tuesday), against 14.4.2025 from the publication.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` `the facts counted from the day the Knesset passed the Law` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 8
-- Where the regulations come later, as they did (16.7.2025), the choice makes no difference: 16.7.2025 either way.
#ASSERT `the commencement day under section 63(a)(1)` (`the facts: published on` (YMD 2025 1 8) `, section 59 regulations in force on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `, section 46 regulations in force on` NOTHING) EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16

§§ `Fork F-C-3: "three months from [its publication or the entry into force], whichever is later" counted from the later of the two (alternative, not taken)`

-- Three months after the later of 14.1.2025 and 16.7.2025, that is after 16.7.2025: 16.10.2025 (a Thursday).
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2025 10 16
-- Then paragraph (2) is 18 months after 16.10.2025: 16.4.2027 (a Friday).
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2027 4 16
-- With the regulations early (1.3.2025): the later of 14.1.2025 and 1.3.2025 is 1.3.2025, three months on: 1.6.2025.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` `the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` EQUALS YMD 2025 6 1
-- On this reading the Law has NOT commenced for propane work on 16.7.2025, and has on 16.10.2025.
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane only` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` `the readings of the regime taken` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane only` (YMD 2025 10 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with the three months counted from the later of the two days` `the readings of the regime taken` EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Fork F-C-4: the Law commences on the last day of the period, or on the day after (alternative, not taken)`

-- Paragraph (2): the period ends on 16.1.2027; the day after is 17.1.2027.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(2) — the day the Law commences for a system with any other refrigerant, under the readings` `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with commencement on the day after a period ends` EQUALS YMD 2027 1 17
-- Paragraph (1)'s three months end on 14.4.2025, the day after is 15.4.2025; with the regulations early the later is 15.4.2025.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` `the facts with the section 59 regulations in force early` `the readings of the dates with commencement on the day after a period ends` EQUALS YMD 2025 4 15
-- With the regulations in force on 16.7.2025 (a date, not a period) the commencement day is still 16.7.2025.
#ASSERT `s 63(a)(1) — the commencement day, under the readings` `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with commencement on the day after a period ends` EQUALS YMD 2025 7 16
-- Work on a system of paragraph (2): 16.1.2027 is not yet, 17.1.2027 is.
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with R134a only` (YMD 2027 1 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with commencement on the day after a period ends` `the readings of the regime taken` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with R134a only` (YMD 2027 1 17) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates with commencement on the day after a period ends` `the readings of the regime taken` EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Fork F-C-5: the commencement day binds from 00.01 (Interpretation Law s.21), not from the first minute of the day (alternative, not taken)`

-- By s.21 the Law binds from 00:01:00 on its commencement day: the moment 00:00:30 on 16.7.2025 is not yet bound.
#ASSERT NOT `s 63(a) and IL s.21 — under the readings, the Law binds work on the system at the moment` `a system with propane only` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 30) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime taken`
#ASSERT `s 63(a) and IL s.21 — under the readings, the Law binds work on the system at the moment` `a system with propane only` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime taken`
#ASSERT NOT `s 63(a) and IL s.21 — under the readings, the Law binds work on the system at the moment` `a system with propane only` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 15) `at` 23 `:` 59 `:` 59) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime taken`
-- Paragraph (2): at 00:00:59 on 16.1.2027 not yet, at 00:01:00 yes.
#ASSERT NOT `s 63(a) and IL s.21 — under the readings, the Law binds work on the system at the moment` `a system with R134a only` (`the moment on` (YMD 2027 1 16) `at` 0 `:` 0 `:` 59) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime taken`
#ASSERT `s 63(a) and IL s.21 — under the readings, the Law binds work on the system at the moment` `a system with R134a only` (`the moment on` (YMD 2027 1 16) `at` 0 `:` 1 `:` 0) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime taken`
-- A system of paragraph (1) is bound at any moment from 00:01 on 16.7.2025, a system of paragraph (2) is not until 16.1.2027.
#ASSERT NOT `s 63(a) and IL s.21 — under the readings, the Law binds work on the system at the moment` `a system with R134a only` (`the moment on` (YMD 2025 7 16) `at` 12 `:` 0 `:` 0) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime taken`
-- The day-level answer on the commencement day is TRUE, on the whole of the day (the reading taken counts the whole day).
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with propane only` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS TRUE

§§ `Fork F-C-6a: a system with refrigerants of both kinds`

-- A system with a lawful propane (paragraph (1)) and a lawful R134a (paragraph (2)).
-- Reading taken (any refrigerant as stated in (1) puts it in (1)): from 16.7.2025.
#ASSERT `work on` `a system with propane and R134a` `on` (YMD 2025 7 16) EQUALS TRUE
-- Reading: paragraph (1) only if EVERY refrigerant is as stated in it, so the later date, 16.1.2027, governs.
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane and R134a` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system governed by the later paragraph` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane and R134a` (YMD 2027 1 15) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system governed by the later paragraph` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane and R134a` (YMD 2027 1 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system governed by the later paragraph` EQUALS TRUE
-- Reading: the text does not say, so between the two dates it refuses; outside them it answers.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane and R134a` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system refused` BECAUSE "the text of section 63(a)(1) and (2) does not say which paragraph governs a system with refrigerants of both kinds"
#ASSERT NOT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane and R134a` (YMD 2025 7 15) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system refused`
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane and R134a` (YMD 2027 1 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system refused`
-- A system whose refrigerants are all of one paragraph is not mixed, whatever the reading.
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane and isobutane` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system governed by the later paragraph` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with propane and isobutane` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system refused` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with R134a and an unlisted gas` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system governed by the later paragraph` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with R134a and an unlisted gas` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a mixed system refused` EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Fork F-C-6b: a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted by law`

-- Reading taken: such a refrigerant is "not as stated in paragraph (1)", so paragraph (2) governs (tested above).
-- Reading: the text does not say which paragraph governs it: refused between the two dates, answered outside them.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with unlawful propane only` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a listed refrigerant of unlawful use refused` BECAUSE "the text of section 63(a)(1) and (2) does not say which paragraph governs a listed refrigerant whose use is not permitted by law"
#ASSERT NOT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with unlawful propane only` (YMD 2025 7 15) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a listed refrigerant of unlawful use refused`
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with unlawful propane only` (YMD 2027 1 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a listed refrigerant of unlawful use refused`
-- A system with a lawful and an unlawful listed refrigerant: its first refrigerant is as stated in (1), and "any" stops there.
#ASSERT `s 63(a) — under the readings, the Law has commenced for work on the system` `a system with lawful propane and unlawful isobutane` (YMD 2025 7 16) `the facts as the sources give them` `the readings of the dates taken` `the readings of the regime with a listed refrigerant of unlawful use refused` EQUALS TRUE

